WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.420
NASA now tracks 6-8 starship tanker flights for Artemis, not 22. This is SpaceX Daily, episode

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:13.660
141. Super heavy rolls at starbase, falcon 9 from vandenberg, starlink in Ukraine, then

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:19.040
the counterpoint, the engineering deep dive, and a week in review. Jeremy Parsons, manager

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:25.100
of the Artemis program, told the Artemis acceleration event on October 23, that NASA is not tracking

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.900
the aerospace safety advisory panel tanker count.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:33.900
A recap on Reddit recorded the Q&amp;A, when a reporter asked which estimate the agency considers

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:34.720
more realistic.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.480
Parsons said current planning follows SpaceX, if propellant transfer efficiency.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:45.420
The share of fuel that actually arrives in the human landing system, or HLS, meets expectations.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:50.400
He said the coming in-space fuel transfer test is what will freeze the tanker total.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:56.400
Losing 5 or 10% of the fuel during transfer, he noted, changes the tanker tally directly.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:02.220
He also said the V3 Starships extra performance will move the number, since each flight that

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:05.520
halls more payload cuts how much propellant Earth has to send.

00:01:06.459 --> 00:01:09.939
Super Heavy Booster 22 rolled toward the Starbase launch pad.

00:01:10.539 --> 00:01:15.959
Video posted on X, not independently confirmed, shows it passing the highway site in transport

00:01:15.959 --> 00:01:18.859
configuration ahead of planned static fire testing.

00:01:18.859 --> 00:01:22.459
when the first stage engines light while the vehicle is held down.

00:01:23.079 --> 00:01:27.179
The move puts the first stage in position for the next integrated flight test campaign.

00:01:28.397 --> 00:01:35.997
Vandenberg's Space Force Base saw Falcon 9 flight that brought California's 2026 launch total even with the state's previous yearly high.

00:01:36.617 --> 00:01:40.917
Ventura County Star reports the mission added one more successful flight to the tally,

00:01:41.337 --> 00:01:44.677
with another launch from the same site already scheduled in the coming days.

00:01:44.677 --> 00:01:50.653
Starlink received a public push from Elon Musk on October 25th, when he posted

00:01:50.653 --> 00:01:55.773
on X that users should try it for reliable internet in any location. The brief message

00:01:55.773 --> 00:02:01.582
highlighted connectivity where ordinary ground infrastructure is absent. An iPhone demonstration

00:02:01.582 --> 00:02:07.962
of a GROC voice shortcut drew a one-word reply from Elon Musk on October 25th. Cool. The

00:02:07.962 --> 00:02:13.062
exchange showed the model settling into mobile workflows. SpaceX and Tesla are the subject

00:02:13.062 --> 00:02:17.602
of combination talks Elon Musk is exploring, according to the Kuwait Times.

00:02:18.202 --> 00:02:22.382
The discussion centers on structural and operational integration between the two companies.

00:02:23.455 --> 00:02:28.875
Philip Securities raised its rating on SpaceX public shares to strong buy on October 24th.

00:02:29.295 --> 00:02:35.115
Market Beat reported the move the same day it took effect, citing the firm's view of the company's growth trajectory.

00:02:36.136 --> 00:02:39.816
Commercial-starling terminals used for offensive drone strikes in Ukraine

00:02:39.816 --> 00:02:45.276
led Elon Musk to say on October 24 that SpaceX had closed the terms of service

00:02:45.276 --> 00:02:45.876
loophole.

00:02:46.376 --> 00:02:51.276
BBC reports Ukrainian officials confirmed that speeds on both Starlink and Starsheald,

00:02:51.636 --> 00:02:54.896
the government network, had returned to pre-restriction levels.

00:02:55.476 --> 00:02:59.616
Connections remained stable above 400 kilometers per hour for moving equipment.

00:03:00.236 --> 00:03:04.736
Zaelin Ski said getting that capacity back helped frontline logistics and the fight against

00:03:04.736 --> 00:03:06.236
jet-powered Shahed drones.

00:03:06.236 --> 00:03:11.776
Musk reiterated that star shield stays under U.S. government control, split from civilian

00:03:11.776 --> 00:03:12.336
starlink.

00:03:12.596 --> 00:03:16.916
A week of slower service had already weighed on drone operations before the restore.

00:03:18.077 --> 00:03:22.717
Worth keeping an eye on, Ukrainian defense officials and advisers branded Musk's restriction

00:03:22.717 --> 00:03:28.177
story very strange, because speed and geographic limits already stopped commercial terminals from

00:03:28.177 --> 00:03:28.737
deep strikes.

00:03:29.357 --> 00:03:35.037
Sergei Beskresnov, a Ukrainian presidential adviser, said the terminals on Ukrainian soil top

00:03:35.037 --> 00:03:39.597
up out at 70 to 90 kilometers per hour and will not work on Russian territory.

00:03:40.097 --> 00:03:44.357
The clash leaves uncertainty over enforcement boundaries between the civilian star-linked

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:49.297
network and the separately controlled star-shield system, and over how terms of service rules

00:03:49.297 --> 00:03:51.237
are applied in active conflict zones.

00:03:52.215 --> 00:03:56.835
What converts a tanker plan from a spreadsheet into a flight manifest is the engineering

00:03:56.835 --> 00:03:59.395
reality of how much propellant actually arrives.

00:04:00.015 --> 00:04:04.995
The in-space transfer test will measure boil-off, allige, and residuals rather than leave

00:04:04.995 --> 00:04:10.695
them as paper allowances. Those three are different physics, and they add. Boyloff is heat

00:04:10.695 --> 00:04:15.895
turning cryogenic liquid into gas you cannot use as dense fluid. Liquid methane lives

00:04:15.895 --> 00:04:22.175
near 111 Kelvin, and liquid oxygen near 90, so a tanker in orbit is a thermos sitting

00:04:22.175 --> 00:04:29.315
in sunlight. The solar constant is about 1,360 watts per square meter. Multi-layer insulation,

00:04:29.315 --> 00:04:34.175
station, stacked reflective films with vacuum between them, cuts the heat leak, but it never

00:04:34.175 --> 00:04:34.915
reaches zero.

00:04:35.415 --> 00:04:39.975
Every watt that remains turns a trickle of liquid into vapor, which you vent as lost

00:04:39.975 --> 00:04:42.355
mass or accept as rising tank pressure.

00:04:42.975 --> 00:04:48.395
A waiting tanker loops through roughly 90 minute low earth orbits, sun and shadow, and if

00:04:48.395 --> 00:04:51.655
the campaign needs many ships, the early arrivals wait longer.

00:04:52.335 --> 00:04:57.415
Weight time feeds boil-off, boil-off feeds extra tanker demand, and extra tankers feed

00:04:57.415 --> 00:04:58.015
weight time.

00:04:58.575 --> 00:04:59.695
Olig is freefall.

00:05:00.355 --> 00:05:04.295
On the ground, gravity parks liquid at the bottom of a tank and gas at the top.

00:05:04.855 --> 00:05:07.815
In orbit, liquid and vapor mix and pumps want liquid.

00:05:08.295 --> 00:05:13.115
If the outlet swallows a bubble, the pump starves on vapor and the lander does not get dense

00:05:13.115 --> 00:05:13.515
fluid.

00:05:14.095 --> 00:05:18.795
Settling thrusters give the stack a tiny acceleration so liquid collects at the aft end.

00:05:19.235 --> 00:05:23.935
And header tanks, small vessels kept full, give the pumps a guaranteed gulp of liquid.

00:05:23.935 --> 00:05:29.275
Neither is free, because a settling burn spends some of the same methane and liquid oxygen.

00:05:29.935 --> 00:05:32.375
Methylox for short, that you came to deliver.

00:05:33.095 --> 00:05:34.195
Residuals are geometry.

00:05:34.975 --> 00:05:40.515
Pipes, valves, filters, and tank sums hold a volume that does not shrink just because you wish it would.

00:05:41.095 --> 00:05:44.695
Ordinary plumbing can leave on the order of one or two percent of a load behind.

00:05:45.295 --> 00:05:48.075
A larger share of a small transfer than of a large one.

00:05:48.715 --> 00:05:51.435
Line volume is roughly pipe length times cross-section.

00:05:51.435 --> 00:05:56.895
So short, well-drained transfer lines beat long skinny ones that trap liquid in every bend.

00:05:57.495 --> 00:06:01.775
Added velocity equals exhaust velocity times the natural log of mass ratio.

00:06:02.355 --> 00:06:05.955
The stacks mass at the start of a burn divided by its mass at the end.

00:06:06.575 --> 00:06:12.535
Exhaust velocity is specific impulse times standard gravity, 9.81 meters per second squared.

00:06:13.075 --> 00:06:18.555
Specific impulse in plane terms is how many seconds an engine can hold a thrust equal to its own weight.

00:06:18.555 --> 00:06:24.355
A typical methalox vacuum engine sits on the order of 380 seconds of specific impulse,

00:06:24.955 --> 00:06:28.415
about 3,700 meters per second of exhaust speed.

00:06:28.995 --> 00:06:33.135
Constantine Cielkovsky wrote that log relationship down in 1903.

00:06:33.775 --> 00:06:40.775
A mass ratio near 2.7, the base of natural logs raised to 1, by only that one exhaust velocity

00:06:40.775 --> 00:06:41.595
of added speed.

00:06:42.075 --> 00:06:45.955
Fall short on the propellant that actually sits in the lander and you miss on the log.

00:06:46.355 --> 00:06:47.495
Not on a straight line.

00:06:47.495 --> 00:06:52.715
The repair is more mass launched from Earth, flown on extra tankers that each burn an

00:06:52.715 --> 00:06:57.355
ascent load of their own, a geometric series rather than a line of equal trucks.

00:06:57.835 --> 00:07:02.915
A depot that stays nearly full beats a chain of leaky handoffs because every extra coupling

00:07:02.915 --> 00:07:05.415
is another chance to fall off the mass ratio.

00:07:05.995 --> 00:07:11.695
The magic wand number is methane and oxygen as industrial fluids, cheap molecules against

00:07:11.695 --> 00:07:13.855
the mass that finally sits in the lander.

00:07:13.855 --> 00:07:19.695
The idiot index, how many times the finished service costs over those raw molecules, stays

00:07:19.695 --> 00:07:22.855
high until wasted propellant stops ordering extra flights.

00:07:23.335 --> 00:07:26.835
Because another ascent repeats engines, tanks, and range time.

00:07:27.375 --> 00:07:31.075
Keep transfer waste small, and the next tanker is mostly cheap fluid.

00:07:31.615 --> 00:07:35.635
Let it run, and you buy another whole flight to replace inventory that left as gas.

00:07:36.395 --> 00:07:41.835
Later vehicles that loft more usable methalocks per trip, cut how often you pay that overhead.

00:07:41.835 --> 00:07:47.075
The same logic that made Falcon 9 re-use the point once first stage recovery worked.

00:07:47.515 --> 00:07:52.175
Until hardware transfers an orbit, boil off, allage, and residuals are estimates.

00:07:52.795 --> 00:07:57.595
After the demo, they are data, and the architecture can hold still while the manifest moves.

00:07:58.315 --> 00:08:04.275
Turning to the past seven days, reuse, catch hardware, and the lunar cabin were the threads that kept repeating.

00:08:04.275 --> 00:08:11.495
Falcon 9 booster B1063 reached its 36th flight, stretching the mark for a reused first stage.

00:08:11.895 --> 00:08:16.475
SpaceX prepared to attempt catches of both the super heavy booster and the starship upper

00:08:16.475 --> 00:08:22.255
stage on flight 15. NASA released the first public starship cabin images, and those pictures

00:08:22.255 --> 00:08:28.515
keep both 2028 lunar landing options alive. Before we go, the first on-orbit methalox

00:08:28.515 --> 00:08:33.755
handoff is the next empirical page this program has to write. That covers everything worth

00:08:33.755 --> 00:08:43.735
knowing about SpaceX today. SPC-X closed Friday at $147.49, up 1.9%. I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

